      "spam": false,
      "value": "what I think you're meaning is you want a seperate UI for Desktop mode, than what VR users have yes?\n\nThe menu for VR is easy to use, easily accessable.  The sliding selections are the only thing I'd like to get changed.  Sometimes it's hard to click on something because it thinks I want to slide it instead.\n\nKeyboard Emotes?  yes!  or many customizeable controller options for Touch and Vive (Touch still has some unused buttons)\n\nLooped Emotes would be nice, like Dancing!\n\nText.. yea, I know some people who prefer that.  High Fidelity doesn't have it, but there's an addon you can get that can.  Very handy (though clunky)\n\nWhispering I can agree with.\n\nand Yes GPU would be Ideal.  Some aspects are GPU, like models and such, but physics are CPU\n\nHowever... I think you should put these all into their own entries, so they can be voted on individually (and some of these already exist on Canny, you should find and upvote them.)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
